e messages array.</p> </li> </ul> <p>The endpoint routes requests that share the same prefix to the same instance and, when that instance hosts more than one copy of the invoked inference component, to the same copy. Set this value to cover shared content (such as system prompts) plus enough unique content to distribute workloads across instances and copies.</p>","    * @public","    */","   PrefixLength?: number | undefined;"," ","   /**","-   * <p>The maximum number of in-flight requests on the target instance before the endpoint routes to another instance. Required when <code>RoutingStrategy</code> is <code>PREFIX_AWARE</code>. When in-flight requests on the prefix-selected instance reach this threshold, the endpoint routes the request to an instance with more available capacity.</p>","+   * <p>The number of in-flight requests on the selected instance or inference component copy at which the endpoint routes a request to another copy or instance. Required when <code>RoutingStrategy</code> is <code>PREFIX_AWARE</code>.</p> <p>On an endpoint without inference components, the endpoint compares this threshold with the number of in-flight requests on the selected instance. When that number reaches the threshold, the endpoint routes the request to another instance.</p> <p>On an endpoint with inference components, the endpoint compares this threshold with the number of in-flight requests on the selected copy of the invoked inference component. Requests to other inference components on the same instance don't count. When the instance hosts more than one copy of the inference component, the endpoint routes requests that share a prefix to the same copy and, while that copy has reached the threshold, to another copy on the instance that is under the threshold. When every copy on the instance has reached the threshold, the endpoint routes the request to another instance.</p> <p>The threshold applies to every instance and every copy of every inference component in the production variant, so choose a value that suits the instance or copy that can serve the fewest concurrent requests.</p>","    * @public","    */","   ConcurrencyThreshold?: number | undefined;","@@ -4293,7 +4307,7 @@ export interface PrefixAwareRoutingConfig {","  */"," export interface ProductionVariantRoutingConfig {","   /**","-   * <p>Sets how the endpoint routes incoming traffic:</p> <ul> <li> <p> <code>LEAST_OUTSTANDING_REQUESTS</code>: The endpoint routes requests to the specific instances that have more capacity to process them.</p> </li> <li> <p> <code>RANDOM</code>: The endpoint routes each request to a randomly chosen instance.</p> </li> <li> <p> <code>PREFIX_AWARE</code>: The endpoint routes requests that share the same prompt prefix to the same instance. When the number of in-flight requests on the selected instance reaches the configured threshold, the endpoint routes the request to an instance with more available capacity.</p> </li> </ul>","+   * <p>Sets how the endpoint routes incoming traffic:</p> <ul> <li> <p> <code>LEAST_OUTSTANDING_REQUESTS</code>: The endpoint routes requests to the specific instances that have more capacity to process them.</p> </li> <li> <p> <code>RANDOM</code>: The endpoint routes each request to a randomly chosen instance.</p> </li> <li> <p> <code>PREFIX_AWARE</code>: The endpoint routes requests that share the same prompt prefix to the same instance and, when that instance hosts more than one copy of the invoked inference component, to the same copy. When the number of in-flight requests on the selected instance or copy reaches the <code>ConcurrencyThreshold</code> value, the endpoint routes the request to another copy on that instance or to another instance. The endpoint applies prefix-aware routing only when two or more instances can serve the request.</p> </li> </ul>","    * @public","    */","   RoutingStrategy: RoutingStrategy | undefined;","@@ -4441,6 +4455,12 @@ export interface ProductionVariant {","    * @public","    */"